    <!-- Grid-tile mime label (Downloads + Captured + Cloud grids). TEXT, not a
         pill — the grid meta row now speaks ONE visual language, the same
         weighted-text hierarchy the list rows use (MimePrimaryLabel below):
         the type takes full-strength light ink, the duration/size after it
         stays at ~88% white, and a "·" separates them. Legibility over bright
         artwork is carried by the bottom_scrim + a drop shadow (set per-tile in
         the adapters, which also swap both to theme ink on the scrim-less
         fallback "card" tiles), NOT by a background behind this one token.
         History — the fill was iterated SIX times before the form was
         questioned: solid coral colorPrimaryContainer (shouted the type on
         every tile), 15% white (invisible on bright frames), 50% black (too
         faint to register as a badge), +1dp stroke (worse), 80% black, then a
         per-theme #99/#E6 split. Every round tuned contrast; none fixed the
         actual problems — a filled box was the heaviest mark in the row while
         carrying the LEAST information (a Downloads grid is ~90% "VIDEO", so
         the token is near-zero entropy), it mixed two languages with the bare
         text 6dp away, and it needed a per-theme fill for a backdrop (the
         thumbnail) that never changes with the theme. Deleting the box removes
         the whole tuning surface. Metrics match MimePrimaryLabel so list and
         grid read as one system. -->
    <style name="MimePrimary">
        <item name="android:textColor">#F4F4F7</item>
        <item name="android:textSize">11sp</item>
        <item name="android:textAllCaps">true</item>
        <item name="android:textStyle">bold</item>
        <item name="android:letterSpacing">0.04</item>
        <item name="singleLine">true</item>
    </style>

    <!-- Text-only mime label used in the list rows (Downloads / Captured /
         Cloud backup). No chip background — sits inline with the domain on the
         metadata line so it scales naturally with long translations (Russian
         ИЗОБРАЖЕНИЕ, Italian SOTTOTITOLI) instead of pushing the filename
         off-screen. NEUTRAL, not coral (a repeated brand accent on every row was
         noise) — but WEIGHTED: the type takes full-strength colorOnSurface while
         the domain after it stays colorOnSurfaceVariant, so line 2 keeps an order
         (type leads, domain trails) instead of flattening into one grey. The
         "VIDEO · youtube.com" unit reads as type-then-source without a colour
         shout; bold + caps + letter-spacing reinforce the type token. -->
    <style name="MimePrimaryLabel">
        <item name="android:textColor">?attr/colorOnSurface</item>
        <item name="android:textSize">11sp</item>
        <item name="android:textAllCaps">true</item>
        <item name="android:textStyle">bold</item>
        <item name="android:letterSpacing">0.04</item>
        <item name="singleLine">true</item>
    </style>

    <style name="MimeTertiary">
        <item name="android:background">@drawable/rounded_secondary</item>
        <item name="android:textColor">?attr/colorOnSecondaryContainer</item>
        <item name="android:textSize">12sp</item>
    </style>

